                <pb facs="0482" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/15896: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-17T00:00:00+01:00">October 17,
                        1941—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received October 17—7:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4964. My 4820, October 9, midnight. Foreign Office informed the Embassy this
                    afternoon that some days ago the Soviet Government had indicated its approval of
                    the draft tripartite treaty between Great Britain, Russia and Iran without any
                    suggestion for changes and with apologies for the delay in answering. The Soviet
                    Ambassador at Tehran is said to have received appropriate instructions and
                    negotiations between the three Governments on the the British draft treaty are
                    said to be practically under way.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
